{
  "dom_id": "step-q274927",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given that $X$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, $Y$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, and $Z$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, in which of the following expressions are the Hadamard products well-defined?\n\nI. $XY⊙Z$\n\nII. $YX⊙{Z}^{T}$\n\nIII. $(XY)^{T}⊙Z$",
  "worked_solution": "The Hadamard product of two matrices (or vectors) is only defined if they have the same dimensions.\n\nLet's consider each expression in turn:\n\n- The dimensions of $XY$ are $2\\times 2,$ and the dimensions of $Z$ are $4\\times 4.$ Hence, the Hadamard product in expression I is *not* well-defined.\n\n- The dimensions of $YX$ are $4\\times 4,$ and the dimensions of ${Z}^{T}$ are $4\\times 4.$ Hence, the Hadamard product in expression II is well-defined.\n\n- The dimensions of $(XY)^{T}$ are $2\\times 2,$ and the dimensions of $Z$ are $4\\times 4.$ Hence, the Hadamard product in expression III is *not* well-defined.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
